  "description": "LIV-101 fishing-village NPC roster (Dawnreach Isle town, `town_havenreach`). Pure data: every return string is a dialogue id resolved by dialogues.json; no per-NPC JS. `npcSpriteId` (LIV-81) names the NPC's own 32x32 actor sprite in the sprite catalog; the renderer resolve order is `npcSpriteId > spriteId > type`, so an unknown/missing `npcSpriteId` falls back to the shared `spriteId`. `spriteId` resolves through the existing actor pipeline (asset sprites index); `renderTheme` remains the fallback tint until every NPC sprite lands. `portraits` (LIV-81) maps each dialogue expression ({neutral,warm,urgent}) to a 48x48 bust asset id, selected by the playing dialogue stage's `expression`; `svgCode`/`portraitEmoji` stay as the migration fallback. `aiType` is the neutral-entity dispatch key (stationary|wander). Quest wiring is unchanged: the 8 named cast keep their ids so `quests.json` `giverNpcId`/`turnInNpcId` resolve; the 5 ambient Shore folk are wander-only flavor with no quest hooks.",
